        "original_id": "0369c6b2-8118-5632-bfd4-41d532095c12",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Marc Rosset, Guillermo Vilas, Renzo Furlan\n- Events: 1992 Olympic Games, 1994 Waldbaum's Hamlet Cup – Singles, 1976 Bavarian Tennis Championships – Singles\n- Places: Switzerland, Argentina\n- Roles: defending champion, former professional tennis player, retired professional tennis player\n\nFacts:\n- Guillermo Vilas was born on 17 August 1952 and is a retired professional tennis player from Argentina.\n- Marc Rosset was born on 7 November 1970 and is a former professional tennis player from Switzerland.\n- Guillermo Vilas finished as the Grand Prix tennis circuit season No. 1 in 1974, 1975, and 1977.\n- Guillermo Vilas won four majors, seven Grand Prix Super Series titles, and 62 ATP titles.\n- Guillermo Vilas was the defending champion for the 1976 Bavarian Tennis Championships – Singles, but he did not participate that year.\n- Marc Rosset won the men's singles gold medal at the 1992 Olympic Games.\n- Marc Rosset was the defending champion at the 1994 Waldbaum's Hamlet Cup – Singles, but he lost in the second round to Renzo Furlan.",
